<Description>
<![CDATA[Work Register: internal Output]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Null" DataType="DateTime" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Null Date and Time (amount of time = 0)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT2" DataType="DateTime" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT2 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT1" DataType="DateTime" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT1 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT2" DataType="T_ADD" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT2]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT1" DataType="T_ADD" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT1]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output "Out"]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned, and the output "Out" is
not cleared.  We need this Routine to Clear "Out" in that case.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compare: DT1 >= DT2 ?]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
T_GEQ:  TIME -- GREATER THAN OR EQUAL
============================================================
Revision 1.0-01 - Release:  2014-02-28
V1.0-00, 2009-04-23: Initial formal release
V1.0-01, 2014-02-28: Corrected order of parameters in contained T_ADD instructions.
============================================================
Returns TRUE (1) in EnableOut and Out if Ref_DT1 is GREATER THAN
OR EQUAL TO (after or the same as) Ref_DT2
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
NORMALIZE THE INPUT DATES/TIMES
============================================================
This rung adds each of the input Date/Time parameters to a "zero time".
 The T_ADD instruction "normalizes" its output to:
0 <= microseconds < 1.000,000
0 <= seconds < 60
0 <= minutes < 60
0 <= hours < 24
1 <= days <= 31 (and day is valid for calendar month/year)
1 <= months <= 12
valid years are about +/- 5.8 million

Remember that if A >= B, then A+C >= B+C, so we are OK to add.  And
it works if what we're adding is a Date/Time OR an Amount of Time!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Null.Yr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Mo) CLR(Wrk_Null.Da) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.Hr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Min) CLR(Wrk_Null.Sec) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.uSec) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT1,Ref_DT1,Wrk_Null,Wrk_DT1) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT2,Ref_DT2,Wrk_Null,Wrk_DT2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMPARE Wrk_DT1 >= Wrk_DT2
============================================================
Now that the two input parameters have been "normalized":
IF the Wrk_DT1 YEAR is higher,
or if the years are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MONTH is higher,
or if the years and months are the same and the Wrk_DT1 DAY is higher,
or if the years, months and days are the same and the Wrk_DT1 HOUR is higher,
or if the years, months, days and hours are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MINUTE is higher,
or if the years, months, days, hours and minutes are the same and the Wrk_DT1 SECOND is higher,
or if the years, months, days, hours, minutes and seconds are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MICROSECOND is higher or the SAME,
(whew!)  THEN Wrk_DT1 is AFTER OR THE SAME AS (greater than or equal to) Wrk_DT2,
and so Ref_DT1 is greater than or equal to Ref_DT2.

(NOTE: You can type <ALT>- 0 (zero) or click the "tree structure" icon on the toolbar
to close the Controller Organizer tree if you would like a wider view of this rung.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec) GEQ(Wrk_DT1.uSec,Wrk_DT2.uSec) ] ] ] ] ] ]OTE(EnableOut)OTE(Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normally there would be an OTE of "Out" on the rung above,
but because we unlatch (OTU) the Out bit in the EnableInFalse routine,
we need to have all "Out" references be OTL or OTU in order to avoid
an annoying verification Warning (duplicate destructive bit reference).
This warning appears in the user program even if this AOI is locked down....]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Out) OTL(Out) ,XIO(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="DateTime"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="T_ADD"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
